From 3a46551449c2e7fe948c5924b4d3311a17280026 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Geonmo Ryu <geonmo@kisti.re.kr>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 10:14:26 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] nfs: optionally report the capacity of the pools or a
 space reservation

Motivation:
The NFS door reports a fixed total size of 1 EiB and the space used by
all files in the namespace. As a result, tools like df show a
meaningless size and free space, which makes them useless for users and
for monitoring.

Modification:
Add the nfs.capacity.source and nfs.capacity.reservation properties,
which default to dcache.capacity.source and dcache.capacity.reservation.
With 'pools', DCacheAwareJdbcFs reports the total and free space summed
over all online pools. With 'reservation', it looks up the configured
space reservation through SpaceManager (using the existing
ReservationCaches space lookup cache) and reports its size and the space
still available in it.

As NFS doesn't tell the door which export a request is for, the door
can't use the WriteToken tag; with 'reservation', a space token must be
configured, and the door fails to start otherwise.

File counts are still taken from the namespace. If the capacity can't be
determined, the namespace statistics are reported as before.

Result:
Sites can configure the NFS door so that df shows the size and free
space of the pools or of a space reservation. By default, the behaviour
is unchanged.

Fixes: #8275
